course: dictionary
lesson: 11618
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. Appropriation is one of these words. «The council voted on the appropriation of funds for a new library.» The clues are council, voted and funds, so appropriation means money officially set aside for a special use.
explain: «The thief's appropriation of the jewels shocked the whole village.» The clues are thief and shocked, so here appropriation means taking something that belongs to someone else. Always ask what the sentence is about, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: «The designer's use of sacred patterns from another people's culture was called cultural appropriation.» Here appropriation means using parts of another group's culture as your own, often without respect. The clues are sacred patterns and another people's culture.
fact: Appropriation is a noun: one appropriation, several appropriations.
fact: «Appropriation» can mean taking something that is not yours, often without permission.
fact: In money and law, «appropriation» means money officially set aside for a particular purpose.
fact: «Cultural appropriation» means using parts of another group's culture, art or ideas as your own, sometimes without respect.
fact: When a word has several meanings, swap each meaning into the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
exercise: «The town hall approved an appropriation of money for a new library.» What does appropriation mean here? | A long, boring speech | Using another group's art as your own | Taking something that belongs to someone else | * Money officially set aside for a particular use
exercise: «The thief's appropriation of the jewels shocked the whole village.» What does appropriation mean here? | Money set aside for a school trip | * Taking something that belongs to someone else | Painting a picture of the village | Sharing a picnic with friends
exercise: Ruby says, «The shop sold sacred patterns from another people's culture and called them its own.» Which meaning fits best? | Making a patterned rug | * Using parts of another group's culture as your own, without respect | Using parts of another group's culture as your own, without respect | Money set aside for a special purpose
test: «The government's appropriation of funds for roads was announced today.» What does appropriation mean here? | * Money officially set aside for a particular use | Stealing a painting from a museum | Taking a car without permission | A kind of dance
test: Sam says, «Cultural appropriation is when people copy another culture's art without respect.» Which word tells you the meaning? | Copy | * Respect | Art | Museum
exam: «The bank's appropriation of the savings was against the law.» What does appropriation mean here? | A type of bank account | Using a new idea from a book | * Taking money that was not theirs to take | Money set aside for a school budget
